Usage: basenc ENCODING [OPTION]... [FILE]

Encode or decode FILE, or standard input, using the selected encoding.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input. ENCODING is one of
--base64, --base64url, --base32, --base32hex, --base16, --base2lsbf,
--base2msbf, --base58, or --z85.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --decode          decode data
  -i, --ignore-garbage  when decoding, ignore non-alphabet characters
  -w, --wrap ARG        wrap encoded lines after COLS character (default 76).
                        Use 0 to disable line wrapping
  -b ARG                legacy baseN selector
      --base64          same as base64 program
      --base64url       file- and URL-safe base64
      --base58          base58 encoding
      --base32          same as base32 program
      --base32hex       extended hex alphabet base32
      --base16          hexadecimal encoding
      --base2lsbf       bit string, least significant bit first
      --base2msbf       bit string, most significant bit first
      --z85             Z85 encoding
      --help            display this help and exit
  -V, --version         output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
